  nextButton: {fileID: 1015302479}
  questions:
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1088209502}
    teachingLines:
    - "A music staff is where notes are written. \nIt has five horizontal lines and
      four spaces. \nNotes can be placed on the lines or in the spaces."
    questionText: What is a music staff used for?
    answerA: Writing notes
    answerB: Changing the volume
    answerC: Ending the song
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nA music staff is where notes are written."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nA music staff is where notes are written. \nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1314948688}
    teachingLines:
    - "The treble clef is a symbol placed at the \nbeginning of the staff. It tells
      the player \nhow to read the notes on that staff. \nGuitar music is usually
      written in treble clef."
    questionText: Where does the treble clef appear?
    answerA: At the end of the song
    answerB: Under the guitar
    answerC: At the beginning of the staff
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nIt appears at the beginning of the staff."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nIt appears at the beginning of the staff. \nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 914023773}
    teachingLines:
    - " A time signature tells the player how many \nbeats fit inside one measure.
      In this game, \nwe will use 4/4 time. That means each \nmeasure needs exactly
      4 beats."
    questionText: "In 4/4 time, how many beats \ndoes each measure need?"
    answerA: 1 beat
    answerB: 4 beats
    answerC: 2 beats
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nIn 4/4 time, each measure needs exactly 4 beats."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nIn 4/4 time, each measure needs exactly 4 beats. \nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 647150609}
    teachingLines:
    - "A quarter note lasts for 1 beat.\r\nThat means when you play a quarter note,
      \nit takes up one count in the measure."
    questionText: How many beats does a quarter note get?
    answerA: 1 beat
    answerB: 2 beats
    answerC: 4 beats
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nA quarter note gets 1 beat."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nA quarter note gets 1 beat. \nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 406544670}
    teachingLines:
    - "In 4/4 time, each measure needs exactly 4 beats.\r\nSince one quarter note
      gets 1 beat, \nfour quarter notes can fill one full measure."
    questionText: How many quarter notes fill one measure in 4/4 time?
    answerA: 1 quarter note
    answerB: 2 quarter notes
    answerC: 4 quarter notes
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nFour quarter notes fill one measure in 4/4 time."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nSince each quarter note gets 1 beat, \nit takes four quarter
      notes to fill 4 beats.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 692374142}
    teachingLines:
    - 'A half note lasts for 2 beats.

      That means it is held longer than a
      quarter note.'
    questionText: How many beats does a half note get?
    answerA: 1 beat
    answerB: 2 beats
    answerC: 3 beats
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nA half note gets 2 beats."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nA half note only gets 2 beats.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 779658411}
    teachingLines:
    - "In 4/4 time, each measure needs exactly 4 beats.\r\nSince one half note gets
      2 beats, \ntwo half notes can fill one full measure."
    questionText: How many half notes fill one measure in 4/4 time?
    answerA: 1 half note
    answerB: 2 half notes
    answerC: 4 half notes
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nTwo half notes fill one measure in 4/4 time."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nSince each half note gets 2 beats, \nit takes two half notes
      to fill 4 beats.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1880736193}
    teachingLines:
    - 'A whole note lasts for 4 beats.

      It is held longer than both a quarter
      note and a half note.'
    questionText: How many beats does a whole note get?
    answerA: 1 beat
    answerB: 2 beats
    answerC: 4 beats
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nA whole note gets 4 beats."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nA whole note gets 4 beats.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1880736193}
    teachingLines:
    - "In 4/4 time, each measure needs exactly 4 beats.\r\nSince one whole note gets
      4 beats, \none whole note can fill the entire measure by itself."
    questionText: How many whole notes are needed to fill one measure in 4/4 time?
    answerA: 1 whole note
    answerB: 2 whole notes
    answerC: 4 whole notes
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nOne whole note fills one full measure in 4/4 time."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nSince a whole note gets 4 beats, one whole note fills the whole
      measure.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1280290872}
    teachingLines:
    - 'A rest tells the player when to stay silent.

      A quarter rest lasts for
      1 beat of silence.'
    questionText: How many beats does a quarter rest get?
    answerA: 1 beat
    answerB: 2 beats
    answerC: 4 beats
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nA quarter rest gets 1 beat of silence."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nA quarter rest gets 1 beat of silence.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1270452314}
    teachingLines:
    - "In 4/4 time, each measure needs exactly 4 beats.\r\nSince one quarter rest
      gets 1 beat, \nfour quarter rests can fill one full measure with silence."
    questionText: How many quarter rests fill one measure in 4/4 time?
    answerA: 1 quarter rests
    answerB: 2 quarter rests
    answerC: 4 quarter rests
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nFour quarter rests fill one measure in 4/4 time."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nSince each quarter rest gets 1 beat, \nit takes four quarter
      rests to fill 4 beats.\r\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 257572029}
    teachingLines:
    - 'A half rest tells the player to stay silent for 2 beats.

      It lasts longer
      than a quarter rest.'
    questionText: How many beats does a half rest get?
    answerA: 1 beat
    answerB: 2 beats
    answerC: 4 beats
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nA half rest gets 2 beats of silence."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nA half rest gets 2 beats of silence.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1417482994}
    teachingLines:
    - 'In 4/4 time, each measure needs exactly 4 beats.

      Since one half rest
      gets 2 beats, two half rests can fill one full measure with silence.'
    questionText: How many half rests fill one measure in 4/4 time?
    answerA: 1 half rest
    answerB: 2 half rests
    answerC: 4 half rests
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nTwo half rests fill one measure in 4/4 time."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nSince each half rest gets 2 beats, \nit takes two half rests
      to fill 4 beats.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1870168123}
    teachingLines:
    - 'A whole rest tells the player to stay silent for 4 beats.

      It is the
      longest rest in this lesson.'
    questionText: How many beats does a whole rest get?
    answerA: 1 beat
    answerB: 2 beats
    answerC: 4 beats
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nA whole rest gets 4 beats of silence."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nA whole rest gets 4 beats of silence.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1870168123}
    teachingLines:
    - "In 4/4 time, each measure needs exactly 4 beats.\nSince one whole rest gets
      4 beats, \none whole rest can fill the entire measure with silence."
    questionText: How many whole rests are needed to fill one measure in 4/4 time?
    answerA: 1 whole rest
    answerB: 2 whole rests
    answerC: 4 whole rests
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nOne whole rest fills one full measure in 4/4 time."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nSince a whole rest gets 4 beats, one whole rest fills the whole
      measure.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 393440974}
    teachingLines:
    - "In 4/4 time, each measure needs exactly 4 beats.\r\nTo complete the measure,
      count how many beats \nare already there, then choose what value is missing."
    questionText: "This measure has 3 beats. \nWhat note completes the measure?"
    answerA: 1 quarter note
    answerB: 1 half note
    answerC: 1 whole note
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nThe measure has 3 beats, so \na quarter note completes the measure"
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nThe measure has 3 beats, \nso it needs 1 more beat to make 4.\nTry
      again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1427166870}
    teachingLines:
    - 'This measure already has 2 beats.

      It needs 2 more beats to reach 4.'
    questionText: Which answer can complete the measure?
    answerA: 1 half note
    answerB: 2 quarter notes
    answerC: 1 whole note
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: 1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nThis measure needs 2 more beats. \nA half note or two quarter notes
      can work."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nThis measure needs exactly 2 more beats to reach 4.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1830205841}
    teachingLines:
    - 'Rests are silent, but they still count as beats.

      A measure with rests
      still needs to add up to exactly 4 beats.'
    questionText: "This measure has 3 beats. \nWhat rest completes the measure?"
    answerA: 1 whole rest
    answerB: 1 half rest
    answerC: 1 quarter rest
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: -1
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nThe measure has 3 beats, so it needs 1 more beat to make 4."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nThis measure has 3 beats, so it only needs 1 more beat.\nTry
      again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1758721185}
    teachingLines:
    - "Longer rests can take up more than one beat.\r\nIf the measure has 2 beats
      already, \nit needs 2 more beats to be complete."
    questionText: "This measure has 2 beats. \nWhat rest(s) completes the measure?"
    answerA: 1 whole rests
    answerB: 1 half rests
    answerC: 2 quarter rests
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: 2
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nThis measure needs 2 more beats. \nA half rest or two quarter rests
      can work."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nThis measure needs exactly 2 more beats to reach 4.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1040843878}
    teachingLines:
    - 'Notes and rests can be used together in the same measure.

      It does not
      matter if the beat is sound or silence.

      The total still needs to equal
      4 beats.'
    questionText: "What notes/rests complete the measure?\t"
    answerA: 1 half note
    answerB: 1 quarter note
    answerC: 1 quarter rest
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: 2
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nThis measure needs 1 more beat1. \nA quarter note or quarter rest
      can work."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nThis measure needs exactly 1 more beat to reach 4.\nTry again."
  - visualGroup: {fileID: 1099734623}
    teachingLines:
    - "When notes and rests are mixed together, \ncount each beat value carefully.The
      goal is \nstill to make the measure total exactly 4 beats.\r\n"
    questionText: "This measure has 3 beats. \nWhat value completes the measure?"
    answerA: 1 whole rest
    answerB: 1 quarter rest
    answerC: 1 quarter note
    correctAnswerIndex: 1
    secondCorrectAnswerIndex: 2
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - "Correct! \nA quarter note or quarter rest can work."
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - "Not quite. \nThis measure needs exactly 1 more beat to reach 4.\nTry again."
  typeSpeed: 0.04
